      "math_academy_id": "q-110676",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n{(2s-{u}^{2})}^{4}=16{s}^{4}+A{s}^{3}{u}^{2}+B{s}^{2}{u}^{4}+Cs{u}^{6}+{u}^{8}\n$$\n\nwhere $A,B$ and $C$ are constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=4,$ $a=2s,$ and $b=-{u}^{2}.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{4}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{3}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{3},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2s-{u}^{2})^{4} & =1{a}^{4}{b}^{0}+4{a}^{3}b+6{a}^{2}{b}^{2}+4a{b}^{3}+1{a}^{0}{b}^{4} \\\\  & =1(2s)^{4}{(-{u}^{2})}^{0}+4(2s)^{3}{(-{u}^{2})}^{1}+6(2s)^{2}{(-{u}^{2})}^{2} \\\\  & \\,+4(2s)^{1}{(-{u}^{2})}^{3}+1(2s)^{0}{(-{u}^{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =1(16{s}^{4})(1)+4(8{s}^{3})(-{u}^{2})+6(4{s}^{2})({u}^{4}) \\\\  & \\,+4(2s)(-{u}^{6})+1(1)({u}^{8}) \\\\  & =16{s}^{4}-32{s}^{3}{u}^{2}+24{s}^{2}{u}^{4}-8s{u}^{6}+{u}^{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=-32,B=24,$ and $C=-8.$ Finally, then\n\n$$\nA+B+C=-32+24-8=-16.\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
